<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan BSPA to tender for 54,000 tonnes soybeans.</title>
<headline>Taiwan BSPA to tender for 54,000 tonnes soybeans.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Taichung division of Taiwan's Breakfast Soybean Procurement Association will tender on Wednesday for a 54,000-tonne shipment of U.S. or south American soybeans, traders said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The breakfast association's Taichung division comprises Sino Japan Feed Corp, Chia Hsin, Formosa Oilseed, Fwu Sow Grain and Tay Shan.  </p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:</p>
<p> Type		     Tonnes   Date/Location</p>
<p>					 U.S. Gulf    Pacific N.W.</p>
<p> U.S.		     54,000   Aug 1-15     Aug 16-30</p>
<p>	 -- or --</p>
<p>					 Argentine/Brazil port</p>
<p> Argentine/Brazilian  54,000   July 26- Aug 14</p>
<p>-- George Hsu, Taipei newsroom (886-2-5080815)</p>
